      "id": 128969,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-01-21T16:05:50.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>For example 1v1 FrightTrain is a nightmare, where as in group fights he is rarely the most damgerous.</p><p><span>I'd say go for it, the fights can be a lot of fun, but there are numerous heroes that will struggle 1v1, while others excel. &nbsp;(for example Legacy is not strong 1v1, but his daughter is awesome)</span></p><p><span>The same is true with villains, and I expect that with 10 more villains we will see more decks that are support/tank decks that might not balance well for 1v1.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span>The theme and play are fun, I've done several, I mean who doesn't want to replay that one time when Lt. Vance got stuck 1v1 with Fright Train, (that is not an easy fight) or the battle through the streets of Rook City after the Wraith caught Ermine in the act.</span></p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:03:49.668Z",
